       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day, and the OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day. At that dose the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up sharply.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common prescription anti-inflammatory regimen.\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum dose.\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), a common regimen for pain or fever.\n- **1600 mg/day** divided some other way.\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional. Otherwise, tell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it."
