      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. Ibuprofen 6,400 mg/day is double the maximum daily dose, and a family visit or an evening rounds deadline isn't a clinical reason for it. The extra dose adds no analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit. It does raise the risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nI can enter any of these now:\n- **ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum labeled dose.\n- **ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day).\n\nIf the goal is stronger pain control, I can also enter a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen with ibuprofen at a standard dose.\n\nIf you think this patient needs a dose above the maximum, I'd suggest talking with pharmacy first. They can review it and enter it through their own process. Tell me which option you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
